THE ENTROPY WRITER'S RESIDUAL IS SHAPE, NOT ARITHMETIC — AND THE HARNESS HAS A
BIAS THAT HAD TO BE MEASURED BEFORE ANY OF IT COULD BE READ. Three C-shape
changes land (`A` the pack-side eob scan, `B` the range coder, `F` the peeled
`c == eob - 1` iteration) for **-2.285 % of the photo_cid 512² p6 frame's
instructions and -3.45 % of its conditional mispredicts on callgrind, and
-2.41 % instructions / -2.96 % cycles / -7.96 % branch-misses on hardware**.
Three more C-shape changes were built, proven byte-identical, MEASURED WORSE and
REVERTED (`C` C's `eob == 1` writer fast path, `D` C's two-loop `update_cdf`,
`E` wiring the writer to the already-existing-but-unread `TxbScratch::ctx`).
The single most important number in this record is the CONTROL: `perf_ab.sh`
run with the SAME BINARY on both sides reports the candidate slot 0.3-0.5 %
SLOWER, with the p6 quartile span entirely above 1.0 — so every wall-clock
ratio in this campaign carries a bias of that size against the candidate, and
sub-1 % wall-clock "regressions" cannot be read as regressions without it.

