host:   r7900x (x86_64-linux, AMD Ryzen 9 7900X, 24 cores).
        A SIBLING LANE WAS LIVE FOR THE WHOLE SESSION: `zenav1-svt--cdef1` ran
        `tools/identity_full_8bit.sh` (one core, `nice -n 19`) throughout, load
        average 1.9-2.8. Every `perf stat` run — both sides — was pinned to
        core 20 with `taskset -c 20`; the callgrind numbers are deterministic
        and contention-immune by construction; the wall-clock A/B is the only
        contended measurement, which is exactly why the base-vs-base control
        below was run under the same conditions rather than assumed away.
        `kernel.perf_event_paranoid` = 1, `nmi_watchdog` = 1 (four events per
        group, no multiplexing at that width).
tools:  perf 7.0.14, valgrind callgrind --branch-sim=yes --cache-sim=no,
        `rust/tools/perf_ab.sh` (21 interleaved paired rounds, order randomised
        per round, neither side niced), a `pstat.sh` paired warmup-delta
        wrapper (median of 5 repetitions of a two-warmup-level delta, so
        process setup / .yuv read / .obu write cancel exactly).
base:   `main@origin` e622a99c2.
C:      reference/svt-av1 @ 3115c0c1 — the PREBUILT oracle in the primary
        r7900x checkout, NOT rebuilt.
cells:  photo_cid 512x512 and screen_terminal 512x512 from
        `r7900x:~/tmp/rc1/yuv` (the .yuv files `callcount_realimg_2026-09-04`
        left), qp 40, still config, presets 2 and 6; plus photo_clic 512x512
        and synthetic `gradient` 256/512 for the wall-clock grid.
data:   benchmarks/entropy_coder_cshape_2026-09-05.tsv

=================== WHAT LANDED, AND WHAT C ACTUALLY DOES ===================

Every item below was found by reading C's source and citing it, not by
micro-tuning the port's existing shape.

**A. The pack recomputes `eob` with a FORWARD full-block scan; C never
recomputes it at all.** `stall_attrib_2026-09-05` named `pipeline.rs:9333` as
the port's largest single mispredict site — 316,928 simulated mispredicts at a
17.16 % rate, 82 % of `encode_block_syntax`'s total — a roughly even
data-dependent `if coeffs[pos] != 0` inside a forward scan of the whole
transform block. The deeper fact is that **C does no work here whatsoever**:
`av1_write_coeffs_txb_1d` (static) takes `eob` as a parameter
(`entropy_coding.c:358`) and the caller passes `blk_ptr->eob.y[txb_itr]`
(`entropy_coding.c:592`), the value the quantizer stored at
`coding_loop.c:441`. The port's pack has no coded-scan eob to carry, so it
recovers it from the coefficients. This chunk replaces the forward scan with
the reverse-scan-and-return already written at `quant.rs:318` (whose branch
mispredicts at 3.10 %), as a private `pipeline::eob_from_scan_rev`.

  THE RECORD'S CENSUS WAS INCOMPLETE, and this is a correction to it: it named
  two sites (`pipeline.rs:9332-9336` and `:9410-9415`, both luma inside
  `encode_block_syntax`). There is a THIRD, identical, in the chroma writer
  (`pipeline.rs:8322-8327` at base, inside `write_chroma_txb`), which runs for
  U and V on every coded block. All three are converted.

  MEASURED (callgrind, photo_cid p6, base -> candA): whole frame Ir
  1,615,400,006 -> 1,607,176,651; `encode_block_syntax` SELF Ir 18,238,244 ->
  9,910,848 and its Bcm 371,547 -> 65,194, i.e. **82.5 % of that function's
  mispredicts removed — exactly the share the record attributed to line
  9333.** Hardware, photo_cid p6: cycles/encode 443,735,363 -> 433,193,020
  (**-2.376 %**) for an instruction change of only -0.540 %, and IPC
  3.4647 -> 3.5299. This is the one place in the profile where a branch fix,
  not an instruction-count fix, was the right lever, and it behaved like one.

  SIZE THE THIRD SITE HONESTLY: `write_chroma_txb`'s self Ir moves only
  6,356,976 -> 6,343,432 at this cell, so the two luma sites carry essentially
  all of the win here. It is converted because it is the same defect on a path
  that runs for U and V of every coded block, not because this cell prices it.

  NOT DONE, and named for the next chunk: carrying the coded-scan eob out of
  the quantizer into the decision so the pack does NO scan at all, which is
  what C does.

**B. The range coder had a helper C does not have, and a hot path C keeps
inlined.** Two findings in one file:

  (i) `svt_od_ec_encode_cdf_q15` (`bitstream_unit.c:279-301`) is FUSED. It
  computes `r_hi = r >> 8` and `temp = EC_MIN_PROB * (nsyms - 1 - s)` ONCE,
  tests `0 < s` ONCE, and subtracts the `icdf[s]` term from `r` afterwards.
  The port materialised `fl = if s > 0 { icdf[s-1] } else { 32768 }` and passed
  it to a private `encode_q15(fl, fh, s, nsyms)`, which re-tested the same
  predicate as `fl < 32768`, recomputed `r >> 8` in its `s == 0` arm, and
  evaluated `EC_MIN_PROB * (n - (s - 1))` and `EC_MIN_PROB * (n - s)`
  separately. **`svt_od_ec_encode_q15` DOES NOT EXIST anywhere in
  `reference/svt-av1/Source/Lib/` — grep returns nothing.** The port was
  mirroring a function the oracle no longer has. It is deleted.

  (ii) `svt_od_ec_enc_normalize` (`bitstream_unit.c:151-174`) is `static
  inline` and contains only the hot path — compute `d`, test
  `EB_UNLIKELY(c + d >= 40)`, store three fields. The flush is a separate
  `static NOINLINE od_ec_enc_flush` (`bitstream_unit.c:110`) whose own comment
  says it is "kept out-of-line to reduce icache pressure on the hot (no-flush)
  path". The port had ONE function carrying both, and LLVM declined to inline
  it anywhere: `OdEcEnc::normalize` was its own symbol at 44,725,701 Ir, 2.77 %
  of the base photo_cid p6 frame, so every symbol written paid a call, a
  prologue and a return around ~10 instructions of work. Split into `#[inline]`
  hot + `#[inline(never)] #[cold]` flush, the symbol disappears from the
  profile entirely (it inlines into `encode_cdf_q15`, `encode_bool_q15` and
  through them into `write_coeffs_txb_1d`) and the cold arm shows up as its own
  `OdEcEnc::flush` at 1,882,969 Ir — 0.12 % of the frame, which is how much of
  that 2.77 % was ever the flush.

  Two smaller things went with it. The port's `output &= mask - 1` before the
  big-endian store is redundant — the carry bit sits at bit `num_bytes_ready*8`
  and the store shifts left by `64 - num_bytes_ready*8`, so it falls off the
  top; C says so at `bitstream_unit.c:132-134`. And the `if self.error { return }`
  that ran on EVERY symbol moved to the cold side: `error` is never set to
  `true` anywhere in the file, and the only thing it could ever guard is the
  buffer write, which is in the flush.

  MEASURED (callgrind, photo_cid p6, candA -> cand3): 1,607,176,651 ->
  1,584,500,175, **-22,676,476 Ir (-1.41 % of the frame)**, Bcm 8,948,419 ->
  8,650,847. This is the largest single chunk in the record.

**F. C peels the `c == eob - 1` iteration out of the backward pass; the port
re-tested it per coefficient.** C's backward pass
(`entropy_coding.c:475-501`) writes the eob coefficient in a peeled block using
`coeff_base_eob_cdf` (3 symbols) and then loops `for (c = eob - 2; c >= 0; --c)`
with `coeff_base_cdf` (4 symbols). The port ran ONE loop over `(0..eob).rev()`
with `if c == eob - 1 { .. } else { .. }` inside it — a loop-invariant predicate
paid on every coefficient. Peeled to C's shape (the base-range escape, which C
writes out twice, is one `macro_rules!` used from both places so it is textually
identical in each).

  MEASURED (callgrind, photo_cid p6, cand3 -> candF): 1,584,500,175 ->
  1,578,489,181, **-6,010,994 Ir**.

=================== THE THREE THAT WERE MEASURED AND REVERTED ===================

All three were built, run and proven byte-identical on photo_cid p6 before
being judged. None is "untried"; each is a null or a loss with a number.

**C — C's `eob == 1` fast path in the writer, +1,924,868 Ir (cand3 -> cand4).**
C skips `svt_av1_txb_init_levels` and `svt_av1_get_nz_map_contexts` entirely for
a single-DC txb (`entropy_coding.c:414-443`), which is why C calls
`txb_init_levels` only at `:452`, below the eob token. The port called it
unconditionally at the top. Ported faithfully — including the two facts that
make it byte-identical (`get_nz_map_contexts` already short-circuits `eob == 1`
to `coeff_contexts[scan[0]] = 0`, and `br_ctx` reads only NEIGHBOUR levels, all
of which are zero when the only non-zero coefficient is the DC). POSITIVE
CONTROL that the branch fires: `__arcane_fill_levels_impl_v3` self Ir, cand3 ->
cand4, 35,521,705 -> 35,099,685. **That is the whole prize: 422,020 Ir, or 0.026 % of the frame —
`eob == 1` txbs are ~1 % of this cell's writer calls — and the added test and
code cost more than that.** Reverted.

**D — C's two-loop `update_cdf`, +17,538,820 Ir (cand4 -> cand2), the largest
single regression measured today.** C splits the CDF update into two branchless
loops (`cabac_context_model.h:98-104`): `for (; i < val; i++) cdf[i] += ...`
then `for (; i < nsymbs - 1; i++) cdf[i] -= ...`. The port runs ONE loop with
`if i < val` inside, and `stall_attrib_2026-09-05` charged 9,688,320 Ir of the
frame to that line. Splitting it made things **1.09 % of the frame WORSE**.
The reading: LLVM was already turning the port's single loop over a
compile-time-bounded range into predicated/vectorised code, and two loops with
runtime trip counts defeat that. **C's hoist is the right shape for a C
compiler and the wrong shape for this one — do not retry it.**

**E — wiring the writer to `TxbScratch::ctx`, +1,342,196 Ir (cand3 -> candE).**
`TxbScratch` (coeff_c.rs:372) carries a `ctx: [i8; MAX_TXB_COEFF_AREA]` field
whose own doc-comment says it exists for the two call sites that used a
`[0i8; MAX_TXB_COEFF_AREA]` stack array — and **it has no reader anywhere in
the tree except the debug poison**, while `write_coeffs_txb_1d_inner` still
declares its own `[0i8; 32 * 32]` and zeroes all 1,024 bytes per call. That is
the "ported but unwired" defect exactly. Wired the way `leaf_funnel::coeff_rate`
already does it (zero `width * height`, hand `get_nz_map_contexts` exactly that
slice), it is a LOSS on this cell: the txbs that dominate photo_cid p6 are large
enough that `width * height` is most of 1,024 anyway, and the scratch's
`Box` indirection is not free. Reverted. **The field is still unread; that is a
real (small) defect and it is now measured rather than assumed to be a win.**

